<Project>

  <!-- This file exists to be found, not to do anything. Do not delete it.

       ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task 2.0.46 defines its own ILRepack target guarded by
       Condition="$(Configuration.Contains('Release')) and !Exists('$(ILRepackTargetsFile)')",
       where ILRepackTargetsFile defaults to $(MSBuildProjectDirectory)\ILRepack.targets. That
       target takes whatever assembly is sitting in the output folder as its input and passes no
       LibraryPath, so on a Release build it re-read the already-merged CellsOfInterest.dll and
       failed with "Failed to resolve assembly: 'Newtonsoft.Json, Version=7.0.0.0'" — while still
       leaving a correctly merged DLL on disk, which is the dangerous part: a packaging step that
       does not check the exit code would ship from a red build.

       The mere existence of this file flips that condition to false and suppresses it. The
       package still imports this file, and the UsingTask that registers the ILRepack task is
       unconditional and runs before the import, so ILRepackMergePLib in CellsOfInterest.csproj
       keeps working in every configuration. -->

</Project>
